==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sɒkət̩̩/}}, {{SAMPA|/"sA:.k@t/}}
* {{audio|En-us-socket.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɒkɪt}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|xno}} ''[[soket]]'', "[[spearhead]]" (diminutive of {{etyl|fro}} ''[[soc]]'' ''[[plowshare]]''), from {{VL.}} ''[[soccus]]''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An opening into which a [[plug]] or other connecting part is designed to fit (e.g. ''a [[light bulb]] socket'').
# {{anatomy}} The part of a [[joint]] that receives a [[bone]].
# {{anatomy}} A [[hollow]] into which a part (e.g. [[eye]]) fits.

